{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f346faf8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022511,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.192086+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.169575+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Real-Time Lightweight Deepfake Audio Detection using Tiny SSL + Lightweight Temporal CNN\n","\n","**BTP (B.Tech Project) — Research Notebook (v2 — improved)**\n","\n","### Objective\n","This notebook implements and trains a **binary audio deepfake detector** (Real vs. Fake / Bonafide vs. Spoof)\n","on the **ASVspoof 5** dataset, designed to be **lightweight enough for real-time / edge deployment**.\n","\n","### Architecture (v2)\n","\n","```\n","Input Audio\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Voice Activity Detection (VAD)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Tiny SSL Encoder (DistilHuBERT, last N layers fine-tuned)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Lightweight Temporal CNN (Conv1d over time, SSL dim = channels)   <- FIXED, see changelog\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Wavelet Block (optional, PyWavelets DWT fusion, from raw waveform)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Self-Attention Pooling (on SSL sequence, complementary branch)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Classifier Head (Linear → GELU → Dropout → Linear)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Real / Fake\n","```\n","\n","### v2 Changelog — why this notebook was modified\n","\n","The original notebook (v1) trained but generalized very poorly: `val_f1` collapsed from 0.58 (epoch 1,\n","already the *best* epoch) down to ~0.47 by epoch 6, while `train_f1` kept climbing to 0.92. Final reported\n","dev metrics were `acc=0.70, precision=0.42, recall=0.94, f1=0.58, EER=23.4%` — far from usable for\n","anti-spoofing (competitive systems target single-digit EER). A full diagnosis is in the accompanying\n","write-up; the **root causes** and **targeted fixes** applied here are:\n","\n","1. **Architecture/axis mismatch (main suspected cause).** v1 reshaped the SSL output `(B, frames, 768)`\n","   into a single-channel \"image\" `(B, 1, frames, 768)` and ran it through an **ImageNet-pretrained**\n","   MobileNetV3-Small. 2D convolutions assume local correlation along *both* spatial axes, but the SSL\n","   \"width\" axis (768 feature channels) has no spatial locality — it's not an image. This corrupts temporal\n","   structure and gains nothing from ImageNet pretraining. **Fix:** replaced with a `Conv1d`-based\n","   **temporal CNN** that convolves only over time, treating the 768 SSL dims as feature channels (the\n","   architecturally correct treatment), trained from scratch (no mismatched pretrained weights).\n","2. **Frozen-encoder train/eval-mode bug.** Calling `model.train()` every epoch cascaded into the *frozen*\n","   SSL encoder submodule, silently re-enabling its internal dropout during training even though its\n","   weights never received gradients — so the classifier head learned on noisy train-time SSL features and\n","   was then evaluated on clean eval-time features. **Fix:** `TinySSLEncoder` now overrides `.train()` so\n","   the frozen part is always forced to `eval()`, regardless of what the parent model does.\n","3. **No real held-out test set.** `eval_df` was hard-coded empty, so the confusion-matrix/ROC/per-class\n","   cell never ran, and the \"final\" metrics were computed on the same `dev` split used for checkpoint\n","   selection (optimistic bias). **Fix:** the dev protocol is now split **by speaker** (no leakage) into a\n","   validation subset (used for early stopping) and a held-out test subset (touched only once, at the end).\n","4. **Training was ~72 min/epoch**, dominated by `librosa` pitch-shift/time-stretch augmentation running\n","   **serially on the main process** inside the training loop (not inside `Dataset.__getitem__`, so it\n","   couldn't benefit from `num_workers` parallelism). **Fix:** augmentation moved into the `Dataset`, so it\n","   runs in parallel across workers; the two slowest ops were also down-weighted in probability.\n","5. **Double-corrected class imbalance.** v1 both used inverse-frequency **loss weights** and (implicitly)\n","   nothing else, biasing the model to over-predict \"bonafide\" (recall 0.94 / precision 0.42 on the\n","   minority class). **Fix:** imbalance is now corrected once, at the data level, via a\n","   `WeightedRandomSampler`; loss-level class weights are disabled by default to avoid stacking corrections.\n","6. **Fully frozen SSL front end.** Off-the-shelf DistilHuBERT is trained for ASR-style phonetic content and\n","   may suppress the very artifacts (vocoder/high-frequency irregularities) that separate bonafide from\n","   spoof. **Fix:** the last 2 transformer layers are now unfrozen with a small discriminative learning\n","   rate, while the rest of the encoder stays frozen (keeps the model lightweight and avoids\n","   catastrophic forgetting).\n","7. Minor: batch size increased (16→48, now that the backbone is mostly frozen and augmentation is fast),\n","   added label smoothing, stronger weight decay/dropout, selection by validation EER (the standard\n","   anti-spoofing metric) instead of F1, and per-class classification report + confusion matrix on the new\n","   test split.\n","\n","**Important:** this environment used to build v2 has no GPU and no access to the ASVspoof5 dataset or the\n","HuggingFace Hub, so the training/evaluation cells below have **not been executed here**. All code has been\n","reviewed for correctness (shapes, imports, control flow) but the actual numeric results still need to be\n","produced by running this notebook top-to-bottom on a GPU (e.g. Kaggle T4) with `DATA_ROOT` pointing at the\n","dataset. Do not trust any stale metrics as if they came from this version — none are reported for cells\n","that require the dataset/GPU.\n","\n","### Dataset\n","**ASVspoof 5 (LA/DF track)** — bonafide vs. spoofed speech utterances with official train/dev protocol\n","files. The `dev` protocol is further split (by speaker) into `val` (early stopping) and `test` (final,\n","untouched) subsets since no public eval-set labels are available.\n","\n","### Reproducibility\n","All experiments use a fixed random seed, deterministic data splits, and full configuration logging (see\n","`CONFIG` below).\n","\n","---\n","*Framework: PyTorch, torchaudio, HuggingFace Transformers, torchvision, timm, PyWavelets, librosa,\n","scikit-learn.*\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"b78a4f44","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.23273Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.232036Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.237015Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.236152Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.026772,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.238545+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.211773+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================\n","# Cell 2: Install dependencies\n","# ==============================================================\n","# Run this once. In Colab/Kaggle/local Jupyter with internet access.\n","# Comment out lines for packages you already have installed.\n","\n","# %pip install -q torch torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\n","# %pip install -q torchvision\n","# %pip install -q transformers>=4.40.0\n","# %pip install -q timm\n","# %pip install -q librosa\n","# %pip install -q PyWavelets\n","# %pip install -q scikit-learn\n","# %pip install -q pandas numpy matplotlib tqdm\n","# %pip install -q soundfile\n","# %pip install -q onnx onnxruntime\n","# # Optional (only needed if you want WebRTC-based VAD instead of the built-in energy-based VAD):\n","# %pip install -q webrtcvad"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"80c98094","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.278472Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:11:54.278205Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:12:23.288472Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:12:23.28750